<section class="block">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head center iv">
      <span class="eyebrow"><span class="tick"></span>Why Pandia</span>
      <h2>Your files stay on your computer.</h2>
      <p>There's no account and no usage tracking. Pandia only goes online to check for a new version once a day, and to fetch the URLs and send the cURL requests you give it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillars iv">
      <div class="pillar">
        <div class="pic">◎</div>
        <h3>Works offline</h3>
        <p>Opening, editing, validating and converting all run on your computer, so Pandia keeps working with <strong>no internet connection</strong>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <div class="pic">⌬</div>
        <h3>Small download</h3>
        <p>Built with <strong>Rust and Tauri</strong> instead of a bundled browser, so the installer is about <strong>10 MB</strong> on macOS and Windows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <div class="pic">▣</div>
        <h3>macOS, Windows and Linux</h3>
        <p>The same views and the same shortcuts on all three, using ⌘ on a Mac and Ctrl everywhere else.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <div class="pic">◐</div>
        <h3>Make it yours</h3>
        <p><strong>19 themes</strong> in light and dark, three row densities and a choice of monospace fonts.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <div class="pic">⎌</div>
        <h3>Hard to lose work</h3>
        <p>Each tab keeps <strong>500 steps</strong> of undo, and Pandia saves backups while you work, so a crash doesn't cost you your edits.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar">
        <div class="pic">⌥</div>
        <h3>Free and open source</h3>
        <p>Licensed under <strong>Apache-2.0</strong> with no paid tier. You can read the code, report a bug or build it yourself.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style is:global>
  .pandia-page .pillars { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); border: 1px solid var(--page-rule); }
  .pandia-page .pillar { padding: 32px 28px; border-right: 1px solid var(--page-rule); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--page-rule); background: var(--page-card); }
  .pandia-page .pillar:nth-child(3n) { border-right: 0; }
  .pandia-page .pillar:nth-child(n+4) { border-bottom: 0; }
  .pandia-page .pillar .pic {
    width: 40px; height: 40px; border: 1px solid var(--page-rule-2); display: grid; place-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 18px; font-family: var(--mono); color: var(--accent-text); font-size: 17px; background: var(--page-bg);
  }
  .pandia-page .pillar h3 { font-family: var(--disp); font-size: 19px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: -0.015em; color: var(--page-text); }
  .pandia-page .pillar p { font-family: var(--disp); font-size: 14px; color: var(--page-dim); margin-top: 9px; line-height: 1.58; }
  .pandia-page .pillar p strong { color: var(--page-text); font-weight: 600; }

  @media (max-width: 940px) {
    .pandia-page .pillars { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .pandia-page .pillar:nth-child(3n) { border-right: 1px solid var(--page-rule); }
    .pandia-page .pillar:nth-child(2n) { border-right: 0; }
    .pandia-page .pillar:nth-child(n+4) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--page-rule); }
    .pandia-page .pillar:nth-child(n+5) { border-bottom: 0; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .pandia-page .pillars { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .pandia-page .pillar { border-right: 0 !important; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--page-rule) !important; }
    .pandia-page .pillar:last-child { border-bottom: 0 !important; }
  }
</style>
